#   against the SDK 26.5 (Darwin 26.x) toolchain — reproduced with a
#   minimal `zig build` project with no Ghostty involved at all. Neither
#   SDKROOT nor MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET env overrides route around it.
#   Zig 0.16.0 does not hit this bug, but can't be used here (see above).
# - A clean from-source rebuild therefore needs an Xcode/SDK combination
#   Zig 0.15.2 can actually link against (e.g. the iOS/iOS Simulator 18.4
#   and macOS 15.4 SDKs below), which on this machine means installing an
#   older Xcode (the macOS 15.4 SDK is already present via Command Line
#   Tools, but the iOS 18.4 SDKs are not) — gated behind a developer's own
#   Apple ID sign-in, not something automatable here.
